d 'LILLARDHAZ': module to estimate simultaneous-equations hazard/probit models with a Gaussian-copula correlation (Lillard 1993)
d
d    lillardhaz fits a two-equation simultaneous model of the kind
d introduced in Lillard (J. Econometrics, 1993): a pair of
d processes -- each a	 binary probit outcome or a continuous-time
d hazard duration -- linked through a single correlation parameter
d rho between their    underlying error terms, estimated jointly by
d maximum likelihood via a Gaussian copula.  Equation 1 (eq1()) may
d be a probit, a    log-normal hazard, or a piecewise
d (linear-log-hazard) Gompertz hazard with an arbitrary number of
d user-specified nodes;    equation 2 (eq2()) is always a hazard,
d log-normal or piecewise Gompertz. With nocorr, the two equations
d are fit under the    (testable) restriction rho=0, which -- as
d shown in The model below -- reduces exactly to two independent
d univariate fits. 
d
d KW: hazard model
d KW: probit model
d KW: Gaussian copula
d
d Requires: Stata version 17
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260925
d
d Author:  Nobutaka Fukuda,   Tohoku University
d Support: email  nobutaka.fukuda@@tohoku.ac.jp
d
f lillardhaz.ado
f lillardhaz.sthlp
f ../_/_lillardhaz_pgomp.ado
f lillardhaz_d0.ado
f lillardhaz_p.ado
